# Project context

- Decentraland SDK7 reference lives under `/dclcontext` and via `cursor.config`.
- **UI Component Kit:** before creating or editing any `Layer` / zone UI, read and follow `.cursor/skills/ui-component-kit/SKILL.md`.
- **Stock assets:** after installing/upgrading `@stom66/dcl-ui-component-kit` in any project, ensure `assets/images/ui-component-kit/` exists (run `npx @stom66/dcl-ui-component-kit copy-assets` if not). npm may block dependency `postinstall` (`allow-scripts`) — that is expected; see `INSTALL.md`.
- Hard rules: one Layer = one Zone (`zone: ZoneType.*` / `<Zone type={…}>` — no `ZoneTop` helpers) + optional `inset`; implement `body()` only; forward size/align through `uiTransform` and `uiBackground` only — never Layer shorthands (`backgroundColor`, `borderRadius`, `showFrame`, …); panel chrome via sibling `<Background />` in `body()` (**never nest content inside Background** — keeps zone flex alignment); do not re-mount `ScreenInsetArea`/`InteractableArea`/`ZoneRoot`/`Zone` in `render()`. Setup groups by inset (`layer.inset ?? screenInset`, default `'none'`). Only `ZoneType.Default` gets a centering shell. Prefer `inset: 'interactable'` over deprecated `ZoneType.InteractableArea`. `zIndex` only when the Layer sets it (cross-inset stacking too).
- **Live platform:** do not snapshot `isMobile()` at module import. `colsDesktop` / `colsMobile` and `getLeftZoneInset()` resolve at render; `cols={isMobile() ? 12 : 6}` in `body()` is also live each frame.
- **Zone alignment:** edge / corner HUDs must use **content-sized** body siblings (omit `cols` on lone `ButtonText` / `Label`; no bare full-width `Row` / `Column cols={12}` around a single control). Zone `alignItems` / `justifyContent` only place children smaller than the zone. Panels: size the Layer with `uiTransform`, then `cols={12}` inside that box. See skill → **Zone alignment needs content-sized children**.
- **Component shorthands (prefer over nesting):** on `Text`/`H*`/`Code` use `value` / `fontColor` / `fontSize` / `font` / `textAlign` (not `uiText={{…}}`); on `Background`/`Row`/`Column` use `backgroundColor` for fill and layout props like `flexWrap` / `alignItems` / `padding` / `margin` (not nested `uiTransform` / `uiBackground` when a shorthand exists). `fontSize` takes theme base px (auto-scaled). `fontColor` on text, `backgroundColor` on Background/Row/Column/Label (chip fill), `iconColor` on Icon, `borderColor` for borders. Nested objects remain escape hatches.
- **Widths:** on `Column` / `Label` / `ButtonText`, use **`cols`** for fractional/full width **inside panels/grids** (`cols={12}` = full). Omit `cols` on `ButtonText` / `Label` for shrink-to-content (edge-zone HUDs). `Row` is always full parent width (no `cols`). `cols="auto"` fills leftover row space (equal share among sibling autos); omit `cols` on `Column` for no grid sizing. Do **not** use `width: '100%'` / `'50%'` / … when a span will do — even if an older demo still does. Row `flexWrap` defaults to `nowrap` (overflow); set `flexWrap="wrap"` for multi-line grids.
- **Imports:** always relative (`./`, `../`) under `src/` — never absolute `src/...` paths. Inside `ui-component-kit/`, stay package-internal (do not `../../ui-component-kit/...`). See `.cursor/rules/relative-imports.mdc`.
- **Box edges:** `margin` / `padding` / `position` keys always **top → right → bottom → left**. See `.cursor/rules/trbl-box-edges.mdc`.
- **`ProgressBarImage.contentInset`:** `number` (uniform) or TRBL edges object. Insets fill/track only — not children. Not `textureSlices`.
